      "explanation": [
        "The scheduled entry point supplies current time and selects ACTIVE charges through a named top-50/before/ordered query; expireOne itself checks only the transition. Per-item optimistic-lock failures are skipped. A Charge object is mutated before persistence/outbox calls, so an annotation alone does not establish unchanged in-memory observations on failure.",
        "Direct expireOne invocation bypasses the selection-time check. Strict timestamp comparison and query locking require generated-query/dependency verification. The stale-save test checks the exception and absent dedup write, but not restored object state. Database rollback, caller object restoration, log/metric atomicity, clock boundaries and fairness are separate questions."
      ],
